+Direct WebSocket listeners support app-server's opt-in auth flags, including `--ws-auth capability-token --ws-token-sha256 HEX`, token files, and signed bearer tokens; clients send `Authorization: Bearer TOKEN` on each connection, or, from a browser, offer the subprotocols `codex-app-server` and `codex.bearer.TOKEN`. Requests carrying an `Origin` header are rejected unless it matches a repeatable `--ws-allowed-origin scheme://host[:port]`, which requires `--ws-auth`.
